  "label": "Historical bread consumption",
  "description": "Bread has been a staple food for thousands of years across many cultures, dating back to ancient civilizations such as Egypt, Mesopotamia, and China. Its production and consumption have evolved over millennia, with wheat being one of the most important cereal crops globally. The claim of 'over 5,000 years of eating bread' is historically accurate and contextualizes the long-standing human relationship with wheat and gluten.",
